<h3><strong>National Vietnam War Veterans Day </strong></h3>
<p>March 29 is Vietnam\'s National Veterans Day in the United States. This day was observed in 2012 for the first time to honor the American military who served during the Vietnam War that took place amid 1955-1975. The Vietnam War included Vietnam in Southeast Asia, as well as neighboring countries Cambodia and Laos. Several million people have been killed, mainly Vietnamese civilians.</p>
<p>The conflict began in the 1950s when the conflict between the northern part of the communist country and the anti-communist south intensified. The conflict ended in 1975 with the fall of Saigon and the victory of North Vietnam. The 2017 Vietnam War Veterans Recognition Act establishes a national celebration. However, this is not a holiday anywhere in the United States.</p>
<p>In the United States, memorial events such as wreaths, speeches, and lunches are organized to celebrate this event. Typical locations include the Vietnam Veterans Memorial in Washington, military cemeteries and war veteran medical facilities.</p>
